Farewell the[ migrant] birds and see them at their best shape.
[Why] did[ we] call San Francisco “Old Gold[ Mine]” and NZ “New Gold Mine”[ ?][ We]’[ll] look at the Gold Rush history.
The bar tail Godwit, champion of Long haul flight. They[ can] fly seven and a half[ day] non stop to Y[al]u Jiang. Then[ to] Alaska[ to] breed. At the end of[ August][ will][ fly] eight and a[ half] day non[ stop][ back] to NZ. It is time to farewell the birds. They are[ leaving] for Yalu Jiang in[ March][.] They[ are] in their best shape and the male birds are in their[ pretty] breeding feather[.] Let’s go to Miranda to farewell the migrant birds and[ hear][ their] amazing[ stories][.]
[Th][ames] is a[ peaceful][ quiet] town now. During[ the] Gold Rush era[,] it was a very busy place with Banks, stock market[,] hotels and[ a] lot of people.[ A] certificate from the Mineral School guaranteed[ a] job in other[ countries]. Let’s review the history of Thames.
